### Guide §5.9 Beyond CRUD. VS Code REST Client syntax: click "Send Request" above each request.
### Start the app with the dev profile (demo users, all with the password "demo-password"):
###   ./mvnw -pl spring-app spring-boot:run -Dspring-boot.run.profiles=dev
### The import requests call openlibrary.org: they need internet. Ids assume the demo data on an
### empty database (docker compose -f spring-app/compose.yaml down -v).

@host = http://localhost:8080

# @name librarian
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "librarian@library.test", "password": "demo-password"}

### Preview an import (200): what Open Library knows, nothing saved. Run it twice: the second answer
### comes from the cache, in a few milliseconds
GET {{host}}/api/books/import/978-0-547-92822-7
Authorization: Bearer {{librarian.response.body.accessToken}}

### Import it (201, one copy, Location: /api/books/{id}). Its authors are reused by name or created
POST {{host}}/api/books/import/978-0-547-92822-7
Authorization: Bearer {{librarian.response.body.accessToken}}

### The same ISBN again (409), answered before any call to Open Library
POST {{host}}/api/books/import/9780547928227
Authorization: Bearer {{librarian.response.body.accessToken}}

### An invalid ISBN (400: the check digit is wrong)
POST {{host}}/api/books/import/9780547928228
Authorization: Bearer {{librarian.response.body.accessToken}}

### Overdue loans (200: the demo data has one, Grace's copy of Pale Blue Dot). OverdueLoanJob logs
### the same list every day at 08:00 (library.jobs.overdue-cron)
GET {{host}}/api/loans/overdue
Authorization: Bearer {{librarian.response.body.accessToken}}

### Borrow Cosmos for Alan (201). Then look at the application log: a moment later, on a thread
### named async-N, "Notify member 2: 'Cosmos' is due on ...", written after the commit
POST {{host}}/api/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{librarian.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"bookId": 8, "memberId": 2}

### Actuator: health is public and says only UP or DOWN (and the probe groups)
GET {{host}}/actuator/health

### ...a librarian also sees each check: db, diskSpace, ping...
GET {{host}}/actuator/health
Authorization: Bearer {{librarian.response.body.accessToken}}

### The build (artifact, version, time) and the Java version: public
GET {{host}}/actuator/info

### Metrics: librarians only (401 without a token). The list of names...
GET {{host}}/actuator/metrics
Authorization: Bearer {{librarian.response.body.accessToken}}

### ...and one of them: the calls to Open Library. After the requests above, COUNT is 1: the second
### preview and the import found the book in the cache
GET {{host}}/actuator/metrics/http.client.requests
Authorization: Bearer {{librarian.response.body.accessToken}}

### Request timings for one endpoint, filtered by tag
GET {{host}}/actuator/metrics/http.server.requests?tag=uri:/api/loans/overdue
Authorization: Bearer {{librarian.response.body.accessToken}}

### Not exposed over HTTP, even for a librarian (404): env would show the configuration
GET {{host}}/actuator/env
Authorization: Bearer {{librarian.response.body.accessToken}}
